/-- solkey `SolcArrays.popThenPushSlotIsZeroed` (`solc/SolcArrays.sol`).

solc: array/array_storage_index_zeroed_test.sol — the upstream invariant that a slot
beyond the current length reads as zero: write a slot, pop it, push it back, and it is
cleared.

solkey tags this `@custom:key box`; the port makes its assumptions true
instead, so the diamond also proves that it does not revert. -/
theorem popThenPushSlotIsZeroed :
    Diamond (State.init SolcArrays)
    sol[SolcArrays]{
      storageArray.push();
      storageArray[0] = 7;
      assert(storageArray[0] == 7);
      storageArray.pop();
      storageArray.push();
      assert(storageArray[0] == 0);
    } := by
  corpus_decide

